Keep it up.

Cybercab's ceiling may be set by how much people are willing to travel, not by the size of today's rideshare market.

@JOBhakdi argues that a much cheaper, frictionless ride grows total usage the way cheaper compute grew total computing. Elon is already saying Cybercab will do a majority of all passenger miles wherever it's legal.

That makes valuing Tesla against Uber's market cap backwards. The real comparison is the entire cost of moving people and goods, and that number grows every time the price per mile falls. $TSLA
